      "writtenOn": "2025-01-06T21:49:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1 to Hai. `adb install -r` doesn\u0027t automatically allow an app to install without signatures. In fact `-r` is more like a no-op now. Could you provide an example APK that can be installed without signature?",
      "parentUuid": "2fc2d91e_373c90c0",
      "revId": "7165b28a84c679a4190a3455632dc7280573fd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc2c5286_ec343ce9",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 3183690
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-07T06:06:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@schfan@google.com ：\n\n I have try to install the apk without  signature ,but it can insucessful. But\n\n(1）This is a very low probability problem, and it is not easy to reproduce this problem. I think this should be caused by data inconsistency caused by thread operation of AndroidPackage. We can find that the computePackageStateHash method does not hold pms.installLock. During the installation of the application, the signature information has not been set or we are uninstalling the application and deleting the signature information. In this case, the acquired signature information is empty.\n\n(2)When using the getSignatures method, the AOSP source code will always check whether it is not empty, which should be the process of installing or uninstalling the application. In order to prevent system_server from crashing, we\u0027d better add a non-empty check here as well.",
      "parentUuid": "1c552682_9cb8e5e6",
      "revId": "7165b28a84c679a4190a3455632dc7280573fd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80b6a339_994a8639",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1351609
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-07T17:40:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I think this should be caused by data inconsistency caused by thread operation of AndroidPackage. We can find that the computePackageStateHash method does not hold pms.installLock.\n\n`PackageManagerInternal.forEachInstalledPackage` uses a snapshot inside [its implementation](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/PackageManagerInternalBase.java;l\u003d602;drc\u003db4d6320e2ae398b36f0aaafb2ecd83609d2d99af). I don\u0027t think snapshot should ever expose an incomplete state, and if that really happens the snapshot code inside PMS should be fixed instead.",
      "parentUuid": "dc2c5286_ec343ce9",
      "revId": "7165b28a84c679a4190a3455632dc7280573fd70",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f884a634_82e6e693",
